sequenceDiagram
  participant U as User
  participant CS as Connect Screen
  participant TS as Token Storage
  participant CL as API Client
  participant G as Transport Guard
  participant API as Post Anki API
  participant NAV as Navigation Gate

  U->>CS: Tap Connect (busyRef blocks a second tap)
  CS->>TS: consumeClearReason() on mount
  TS-->>CS: "revoked" or none
  CS->>CL: verifyToken(pastedToken)
  CL->>G: assertSecureUrl(apiBaseUrl())
  Note over G: RISK - host parser accepts<br/>"localhost:x@evil-host" as loopback<br/>and accepts uppercase "HTTP" as if https
  G-->>CL: passes (should refuse, does not)
  CL->>API: GET /daily-push with Bearer token
  API-->>CL: 200 or 401
  CL-->>CS: verified true/false or thrown error
  CS->>TS: setStoredToken(token) on success
  CS->>U: navigate to app home

  Note over CL,API: Later, any screen call
  CL->>G: assertSecureUrl(apiBaseUrl()) again, same risk
  CL->>API: apiFetch(path) with Bearer token
  API-->>CL: 401 token rejected
  CL->>TS: clearStoredToken("revoked")
  CL->>NAV: router.replace to Connect
  TS->>NAV: token presence change also triggers redirect
  NAV->>CS: Connect renders, reads "revoked" once
